'''''Carex caryophyllea''''' is a species of plant in the family [[Cyperaceae]] first described by [[Marc Antoine Louis Claret de La Tourrette]]. Two varieties are listed in the [[World Checklist of Selected Plant Families]]:<ref name=wcsp>{{cite web|title=''Carex caryophyllea'' Latourr., Chlor. Lugd.: 27 (1785).|url=https://wcsp.science.kew.org/namedetail.do?name_id=225358|website=wcsp.science.kew.org|accessdate=26 July 2020}}</ref>
* ''Carex caryophyllea'' var. ''caryophyllea'' — temperate regions of the Old World
* ''Carex caryophyllea'' var. ''microtricha'' {{small|(Franch.) Kük.}} — Far East, Korea, North and Central Japan

